[ti:Unity and Temporality]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:Sidd-hartha.text - Reawakened]

[00:01.83]Son... look at me
[00:05.18]All night you stood there, silent, by my door
[00:09.01]Your legs are shakin', and still you won't sit down
[00:13.16]I know... you're goin' to the Samanas
[00:16.55]Go, then... and if you find the blessing, come back and teach it to me
[00:21.66]And if you find disappointment... come back anyway
[00:25.92]This house will keep a light for you
[00:29.05]Now my own son is gone... and I finally hear you, father
[00:34.43]Evenin'... wherever you are, whatever you're carryin'
[00:39.02]Sit by the water for a minute
[00:40.84]Don't clap... just listen
[00:43.50]This one's for every son who left... and every father who waited
[00:52.10]Listen
[00:59.41]I remember sittin' by the bank, young and proud
[01:02.12]Thought the truth was somewhere past the temple crowd
[01:04.53]Walked away from my father, never once looked back
[01:07.40]Ran with the Samanas, learned to think, to wait, to fast
[01:10.68]Then the silk, the dice, the wine, the merchant's gold
[01:13.67]Kamala's garden, man, I sold my soul
[01:16.05]But I ain't throwin' none of that away now
[01:18.90]River teach what the years disavow
[01:21.63]Every stumble was a stone that built the road
[01:24.44]Every sin I carried taught me how to hold
[01:27.26]One sound echo through the stones and the sky
[01:29.99]Same voice in the leaf and every passerby
[01:32.38]All is one in the current, ooh
[01:36.10]Beginning and the end forever together
[01:40.19]All is one in the current
[01:45.56]Source and the sea, the same water
[01:54.64]Old man Vasudeva never preached a line
[01:57.19]Just leaned to the water like "listen, take your time"
[02:00.09]So I listened, heard the laughter and the cries
[02:02.43]Heard my own reflection lookin' back with older eyes
[02:04.80]Then my boy ran off, took the boat across the shore
[02:07.66]Same wound I gave my father knockin' at my door
[02:10.39]Saw the old man's face in the water when I cried
[02:13.47]Every son's a river leavin' every father's side
[02:15.89]And I let him go, 'cause love don't hold the oar
[02:18.54]Same water carry kings and beggars to the shore
[02:21.60]Om... the bow... the arrow... the goal
[02:24.01]Every wrong turn I took was the river's own road
[02:27.19]All is one in the current, ooh
[02:31.01]Beginning and the end forever together
[02:35.63]All is one in the current
[02:40.30]Source and the sea, the same water
[02:45.83]Grief... and greed... and laughter
[02:48.65]Listen
[02:49.60]Not one voice erased... all of 'em... Om
[02:52.72]Listen close, a thousand voices in the flow
[02:55.52]Mother's cry, the merchant's laugh, the young and the old
[02:58.25]Not one voice is cancelled, every cry belong
[03:00.92]Weave 'em all together and it's Om, it's one song
[03:03.86]Govinda came back knockin' with his questions in his hand
[03:06.40]Forty years of searchin' and he still don't understand
[03:09.19]Picked a stone up off the bank: "I love it as it is
[03:11.95]Not for what it might become"... Govinda, words can't show you this
[03:14.68]Kiss my forehead, brother, then look into my face
[03:17.59]Thousand faces flowin', every one in place
[03:20.45]Didn't need a teacher, didn't need a vow
[03:22.84]Just a smile like the river... and the river's here now
[03:25.84]All is one in the current, ooh
[03:28.54]Beginning and the end forever
[03:31.54]Love is the current, love is the flow
[03:35.58]All is one in the current
[03:37.84]Source and the sea, the same water
[03:44.51]The water laughin'... all of it here
[03:48.97]All is one... all is one
[03:54.22]And the river... keeps on
[03:56.92]
